s","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5790,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:48Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-08T14:17:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T16:53:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124288","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124288","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124288.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124288.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\n\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for contributors:\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\n\nUse of AI must be disclosed and should include a description of how it was used.\n-->\n\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\n- Closes #124279\n\nThe issue describes slow performance when zoomed in. After reproducing the issue, I found the bottleneck was the missing-tile warning processing, even though it wasn't explicitly identified in the original report.\n\nThis PR skips the offscreen processing and drawing of these warnings if they fall outside the current viewport. similar to how it skips the rendering of \"normal cells with a texture\"\n\nWith missing-tile-warning i mean these: <img width=\"1106\" height=\"574\" alt=\"bild\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7a6221c9-2f41-490b-91c9-ed7f0ed769e3\" />\n\n### Tests ###\nGodot v4.8.dev (cd9c5d57f) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors (1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz, 1920x1080 @ 60.00 Hz) - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1692) - AMD Ryzen 7 3700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 15.92 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n**Observations:**\nPanning and zooming the editor in the 2D viewport is noticeably smoother. I also verified that partially visible warnings on the edges of the viewport still display correctly without being prematurely clipped.\n\n**Benchmark**\n\nProject + benchmark script (Script is AI-Generated) : \n[godot-124279-benchmark.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/33208341/godot-124279-benchmark.zip)\n\n**Results:**\nGrid | Before | After | Change\n-- | -- | -- | --\nEnabled | 122.38 ms/frame | 30.24 ms/frame | 75.3% lower\nDisabled | 118.86 ms/frame | 28.03 ms/frame | 76.4% lower\n\n\n\n\n## Additional information\nUsed AI to create benchmarks for improvement, and to localize the rendering loop for the overlay\n\n<!--\nProvide additional information and explanation of your PR, including areas that you are uncertain of or require special attention from reviewers. For examples, please read our pull request guidelines: https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/contribution_rules.html#explain-your-contributions\n-->\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124288/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124288/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}